  "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 2 left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus g right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi>\n<mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi>\n<mo>)</mo></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"d\"><mi>d</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> are unique positive constants. When the equation is graphed in the <em>xy</em>-plane, how many distinct <em>x</em>-intercepts does the graph have?</p>",
