  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. An <em>x</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane is a point on the graph where the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the given equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals 2 left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus g right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, the solutions to this equation are <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"x equals negative d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"x equals negative g\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>g</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. However, <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are identical. It's given that <math alttext=\"d\"><mi>d</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"g\"><mi>g</mi>\n</math> are unique positive constants. It follows that the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"0 equals 2 left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus d right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus g right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus d right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> unique solutions: <math alttext=\"x equals d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"x equals negative d\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>d</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"x equals negative g\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mi>g</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the graph of the given equation has <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> distinct <em>x</em>-intercepts.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>",
